    "Drift is a broad term describing any mismatch or shift between the conditions under which a model was trained and the real-world environment it operates in after deployment.",
    "Drift occurs because the conditions—such as data, relationships between inputs and outputs, user expectations, or the model itself—change over time, sometimes subtly or dramatically.",
    "The three key types of drift mentioned are data drift, concept drift, user/Expectation drift, and model drift.",
    "Data drift refers to a change in the statistical properties of the input data over time, such as a shift in customer support queries from 2020 to include 80% new product feature inquiries.",
    "Concept drift involves a change in the relationship between input and output, such as when customer satisfaction is measured using a new rating scale (e.g., 1–5 stars becomes 1–10) or when the definition of satisfaction evolves (e.g., delivery speed becomes more important than product quality).",
    "User/Expectation drift occurs when users’ expectations of the model shift, like when a chatbot that worked for older users’ direct questions now needs to handle sarcasm, memes, or niche slang.",
    "Model drift refers to the model itself degrading over time due to factors like overfitting to outdated data or failing to generalize to new patterns, such as when a model trained on a small dataset encounters a much larger, more diverse dataset.",
    "Drift matters after deployment because it causes performance collapse, leading to a model’s accuracy, relevance, or usefulness plummeting—like a recommendation system pushing irrelevant items when user tastes shift.",
    "Drift results in user dissatisfaction, as users may disengage or give negative feedback even if the model’s technical output remains unchanged, due to mismatched expectations.",
    "Drift creates feedback loops where poor performance causes users to abandon the system, reducing the data available for retraining and making future drift harder to manage.",
    "Ignoring drift can lead to confident but wrong answers, eroding trust in the model.",
    "Drift can have significant business impacts, including lost revenue, compliance issues, or reputational damage—for example, a fraud detection model missing new types of scams or a healthcare diagnostic tool failing to recognize new disease variants.",
