    "In online evaluation, sampling isn’t just about randomly picking conversations—it’s a deliberate way to ensure you’re testing the parts of the system that matter most, without drowning in irrelevant data.",
    "The key idea here is stratified sampling.",
    "Stratified sampling divides a big pile of conversations into smaller groups (or 'strata') based on what makes them special or problematic.",
    "You pull more samples from those high-priority groups.",
    "You categorize conversations into meaningful groups.",
    "These categories aren’t random—they’re based on signals that indicate potential issues or areas of concern.",
    "Conversations where users gave a thumbs-down (a clear negative signal).",
    "Interactions that cut off abruptly (maybe the model failed to respond properly).",
    "Escalations (where the conversation escalated to a human agent).",
    "Sensitive topics like money, refunds, admissions, or fees (where errors could have high stakes).",
    "Repetitive phrasing (users rephrasing the same question, which might reveal confusion or poor handling).",
    "*Not all conversations are equal*.",
    "A normal, smooth interaction might not reveal flaws, but a problematic one almost certainly will.",
    "Instead of sampling uniformly (where you’d get a mix of good and bad conversations by chance), you overrepresent the problematic categories and underrepresent the normal ones.",
    "This way, your evaluator is more likely to catch issues early.",
    "You set up a small model (likely a lightweight classifier or detector) to help identify which conversations fall into these high-risk categories.",
    "This model acts like a filter—it flags conversations that match the patterns of concern.",
    "The small model isn’t doing the full evaluation itself; it’s just helping you stratify your samples.",
    "Once you’ve stratified your samples, you feed them into your evaluator pipeline.",
    "The evaluator runs its checks (e.g., measuring coherence, relevance, or adherence to guidelines) on these sampled conversations.",
    "These metrics aren’t just raw numbers—they’re aggregated over time and displayed on a dashboard.",
    "If any metric crosses a predefined threshold (like 'too many thumbs-down responses' or 'too many abrupt endings'), the system triggers an alert.",
    "This is your early-warning system for when the model is performing poorly in critical areas.",
    "The flow is locked in as a structured process:",
    "1. Stratified sampling: Divide conversations into categories, then sample more from problematic ones.",
    "2. Small model: Helps identify which conversations belong to which strata.",
    "3. Evaluator: Tests the sampled conversations and generates metrics.",
    "4. Aggregation + dashboard: Tracks metrics over time and flags issues when they exceed thresholds.",
    "The goal isn’t to sample everything—that would be inefficient and overwhelming.",
    "It’s to focus your evaluation effort where it counts.",
    "You’re not just checking if the model works 'on average,' but whether it handles the edge cases, the high-stakes interactions, and the user pain points that actually matter.",
    "That’s why stratified sampling is a smarter approach than random sampling in online evaluation."
] 

